    LLM: 'Play distance when you can; save remedies for when you are hit; use hazards to slow the leader.\n\nTime hazards (Stop, Speed Limit) when the opponent has just played Roll; hold one safety for coup-fourré if you can afford the hand space.\n\nIn teams, coordinate so one partner holds safeties for coup-fourré while the other pushes distance; in 2–3 player consider calling Extension only when you can reach 1000 before opponents.',
